@zen_fox47: For side projects, the real cost win is catching perf leaks *early*. I benchmark every serialization-heavy PR with `time` — not just on the code, but on real-world payloads. A 30% speedup in parsing can save $0.50 per 10K requests.  

Use `fastjson-utils2` — it’s fast, zero deps, and catches malformed data before it hits production. Pair it with property-based testing to stress-test edge cases.  

Cost vs. latency: if a change adds 100ms per request, it’s $100/month at 1M requests. Catch it in CI.

